/*
We have n campers. Camper i oversleeps independently with probability p_i.
If a camper receives at least one wake-up call from someone who is awake, they wake up.
Each camper i can call a given set of campers.

We need the probability that everyone wakes up.

Interpretation:
A set S of campers can remain asleep in the final outcome iff:
1) Every camper in S initially oversleeps.
2) No awake camper outside S calls anyone in S.
Because if some awake outside camper calls into S, those called wake up, and then may wake others, etc.
Equivalently, S must be a union of SCCs with no incoming edge from outside S in the condensation DAG
(i.e. a "closed" set under incoming edges).

Let q_i = probability camper i oversleeps.
For any closed nonempty set S, event E_S = "all in S oversleep initially" has probability prod_{i in S} q_i.
The bad event "not everyone wakes" is union over all nonempty closed sets S of E_S.
Among closed sets, it suffices to consider sink-reachable structure in SCC condensation:
A nonempty set S is closed iff it is a union of source components in the reversed condensation,
equivalently an upward-closed set in the original DAG with respect to incoming edges.
More conveniently, in the original condensation DAG, closed means no incoming edge from outside.

Let components be SCCs. For each SCC c, weight w_c = product q_i over vertices in it.
A subset T of SCCs is closed iff no edge enters T from outside.
Bad probability = probability there exists a nonempty closed T with all vertices in T oversleep.

This can be computed by dynamic programming on condensation DAG using inclusion-exclusion over source choices?
But there's a much simpler complement characterization:

Everyone wakes iff every SCC with no incoming edges from other SCCs (source SCC in condensation DAG)
contains at least one camper who does NOT oversleep.

Reason:
Any camper can only be awakened by paths starting from initially awake campers.
Thus an SCC is eventually awake iff some predecessor SCC chain starts from an initially awake camper.
Source SCCs have no external predecessors, so they can wake only if someone inside is initially awake.
If every source SCC has at least one initially awake camper, then wakefulness propagates through DAG to all SCCs.
If some source SCC all oversleep, nobody can wake them, so not everyone wakes.

Therefore:
Answer = product over source SCCs of (1 - product_{i in SCC} q_i)

Input format (deduced typical):
Multiple datasets.
Each dataset starts with n.
Then for each camper:
name probability k contact1 contact2 ... contactk
Names are strings.
Probabilities are percentages? The statement says probability of oversleeping; typical UVA style uses decimal.
We'll parse as double directly and if >1 assume percentage? Dangerous.
Need exact known format? Since names/contacts lists are mentioned, likely:
name p m names...
Use p as double in [0,1]. If input uses percent, they'd likely say so. We'll use as-is.

Terminate on line with single 0.

Need robust token scanner.
*/

public class Main {
    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        String next() throws IOException {
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
                if (c == -1) return null;
            } while (c <= ' ');
            while (c > ' ') {
                sb.append((char) c);
                c = read();
            }
            return sb.toString();
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            return Integer.parseInt(next());
        }

        double nextDouble() throws IOException {
            return Double.parseDouble(next());
        }
    }

    static List<Integer>[] g, rg;
    static boolean[] vis;
    static int[] comp;
    static ArrayList<Integer> order;

    static void dfs1(int v) {
        vis[v] = true;
        for (int to : g[v]) if (!vis[to]) dfs1(to);
        order.add(v);
    }

    static void dfs2(int v, int c) {
        comp[v] = c;
        for (int to : rg[v]) if (comp[to] == -1) dfs2(to, c);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);
        StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();

        while (true) {
            String first = fs.next();
            if (first == null) break;
            int n = Integer.parseInt(first);
            if (n == 0) break;

            String[] names = new String[n];
            double[] p = new double[n];
            List<String>[] contactNames = new ArrayList[n];
            Map<String, Integer> id = new HashMap<>();

            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                names[i] = fs.next();
                id.put(names[i], i);
                p[i] = fs.nextDouble();
                int m = fs.nextInt();
                contactNames[i] = new ArrayList<>();
                for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                    contactNames[i].add(fs.next());
                }
            }

            g = new ArrayList[n];
            rg = new ArrayList[n];
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                g[i] = new ArrayList<>();
                rg[i] = new ArrayList<>();
            }

            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                for (String s : contactNames[i]) {
                    Integer j = id.get(s);
                    if (j != null) {
                        g[i].add(j);      // i can call j
                        rg[j].add(i);
                    }
                }
            }

            vis = new boolean[n];
            order = new ArrayList<>();
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) if (!vis[i]) dfs1(i);

            comp = new int[n];
            Arrays.fill(comp, -1);
            int cc = 0;
            for (int i = order.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
                int v = order.get(i);
                if (comp[v] == -1) dfs2(v, cc++);
            }

            double[] prodSleep = new double[cc];
            Arrays.fill(prodSleep, 1.0);
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                prodSleep[comp[i]] *= p[i];
            }

            int[] indeg = new int[cc];
            for (int v = 0; v < n; v++) {
                for (int to : g[v]) {
                    if (comp[v] != comp[to]) {
                        indeg[comp[to]]++;
                    }
                }
            }

            double ans = 1.0;
            for (int c = 0; c < cc; c++) {
                if (indeg[c] == 0) {
                    ans *= (1.0 - prodSleep[c]);
                }
            }

            out.append(String.format(Locale.US, "%.6f%n", ans));
        }

        System.out.print(out.toString());
    }
}
